    "gaps": [
      {
        "question": "Why is the first hour of the window busier than the rest?",
        "why": "Provisiond's scheduled rescan of existing nodes ran in two bursts, 00:05 to 00:32 and 00:59 to 01:04 local time, driven by its scheduled pool; the import pool was at zero throughout, so nothing new was provisioned. At the 0.409 node scans per second measured on this fleet a full rescan of 14,000 nodes takes about 9.5 hours against a one-day scan-interval, so roughly 40% of any window is expected to carry it. This one carries it for about 27 minutes of 420, less than that average, not more.",
        "validity": "internal"
      },
      {
        "question": "What happens when real agents time out?",
        "why": "Never exercised. The simulated agents answer in about 0.1 ms and never fail. A timeout holds a Collectd thread for the full retry budget, and the headroom section can only reason about that, not measure it. Response-time sensitivity is the subject of a separate measurement.",
        "validity": "external"
      },
      {
        "question": "Do the delay figures describe what a consumer sees?",
        "why": "They describe when the broker accepted the record, not when any consumer read it; consumer lag on the metrics topic was not measured. The delay capture also ran 05:45Z to 06:10Z, after this window closed, because the topic retains about eleven minutes and nothing from inside the window survived. The Full GC rate that explains its second mode was measured inside the window and matches the capture period, so the mechanism transfers even though the records do not.",
        "validity": "construct"
      },
      {
        "question": "How repeatable are these figures?",
        "why": "One seven hour window on one deployment. The steady-state figures are consistent with the shorter windows measured on the same fleet earlier the same day, but no independent trial exists.",
        "validity": "conclusion"
      },
      {
        "question": "Can this be rebuilt from the repository?",
        "why": "Not exactly. The Core heap of 10240 MiB, the simulator VM at 4 vCPU / 8 GiB and nl6 at v0.28.0 exist only on the running lab; deployments/kfk-exclusive/topology.yml still describes a smaller generator.",
        "validity": "external"
      }
    ]
  }
}